body:
- **Product type.** Hybrid local developer tool made of three parts:
  - a native Linux CLI binary;
  - a Claude Code plugin (hooks + stdio MCP server) that calls that binary;
  - a keyboard-driven terminal fleet console tiled on Hyprland, owed by the 0.2.0 Epoch 6 route entries (matrix#v2-14); no web or graphical frontend.

- **P6 — CLI board, wait/last, verify** (cli). No ARIA. Literal pins over `std::process::Command` assert the non-TTY modes, and the portable-pty outer PTY asserts the TTY-only behaviours, on `ubuntu-latest`:
  - linear static output: under the outer PTY, `waiting: <name>` appears exactly once on stderr and the stream contains no `\r` redraw, cursor-movement or erase sequence (no spinner); under non-TTY the `waiting:` line is absent;
  - `[NN/NN] … pass|fail`;
  - **cli mirror:** a literal pins the caption order (NAME · LIVE · STATUS · WHEEL · DIALOG · CLI), which the terminal fleet console (matrix#v2-14) reuses: the `CAPTION` literal in the root case `list_human_board_is_the_literal_rows` (`tests/cli_list.rs`) and the unit case `board_row_caption_and_default_row_are_the_literals` (`src/human/board/`), chunk 2026-10-11-the-board-viola-list.
  - no SGR under non-TTY / `NO_COLOR` / `TERM=dumb` / `--json`;
  - under the outer PTY, every SGR span sits beside its word (amber only on `DIALOG`, dim only on stale rows, bold only on NAME column values), and `unable` / `fail` carry no SGR; as built (chunk 2026-10-17-cli-output-discipline) `viola list`'s spans are checked under the outer PTY by `cross_list_rows_style_each_span_beside_its_word_on_a_terminal` (bold NAME, amber only on `DIALOG`) and at the unit tier by the `board_row_style_*` cases; dim only on stale rows is proven at the unit tier (`board_row_style_a_stale_row_is_dim_end_to_end_and_only_dialog_is_amber`) and under the outer PTY (the stale-row witness, below); `viola wait` and `viola --help` carry no ESC byte and no lone CR (`tests/support/sgr.rs` `redraws`);
  - C0/C1 escaped (security excerpt, C0/C1 escaping; ratified T5 for `list` rows), checked with `std::process::Command` on `ubuntu-latest`:
    - Setup: human-mode `viola wait` / `viola last` run against a `viola-fake-agent` event whose text carries C0 and C1 control bytes (including ESC / CSI), and `viola list` runs against a `claude agents --json` fixture row carrying the same bytes plus `\n` / `\t`. As built (chunk 2026-10-16-unwrapped-sessions-on-the-board) `viola list` makes one `claude agents --json` read and prints every unwrapped NAME (the row's `sessionId`, never a `ViolaName`) through `escape_row` on one line, held by the `board_row_*` units and by `tests/cross_list_rows.rs` in three modes (piped, `NO_COLOR` / `TERM=dumb`, the outer PTY; the no-ESC assertion in each mode); beside them the row escape is held by unit cases on a recorded CLI version carrying ESC, C1, DEL, `\n` and `\t`, each printed as `\xHH` (`escape_row_shows_every_control_character_as_hex_text`, `board_row_cli_cell`), and the root cases `list_human_board_is_the_literal_rows` and `list_of_a_stopped_wrapper_is_an_empty_board` assert no ESC and no non-ASCII byte on either stream.
    - Pass condition: each injected control appears only in escaped form. In `wait` / `last` text `\n` / `\t` stay raw. In `list` table rows `\n` / `\t` are escaped too (`\x0A`, `\x09`), so every row stays one fixed-width line.
    - Under non-TTY, `wait` / `last` stdout contains no raw C0 / C1 byte other than `\n` / `\t`, and `list` stdout contains none inside a row. Under the outer PTY, the injected controls are escaped, and viola's own SGR stays beside its word only.
  - These stand in for SC 1.3.2, 1.4.1 and 3.3.1, with no conformance claim.
